 N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5a24f8deba99f72728a11066569e94d4869b83afbd955deb77b87a9fb8a41ce0","compact":"087c180aa780f1c5aeb9b92b3d3e38401ed6d428c0680f19972101be0f9f2c59","nasal":"ef728498fecd4211aa1bdf814540629dc6cdc32eba67f3858698b8117d9b4b58"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-7-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":7,"verse":8,"english":"With sharpened arrows resembling the thunder, and endowed with the velocity of the wind, shot from his bow drawn to its fullest stretch, Visnu cut off (Raksasas) by hundreds and by thousands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.537,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-7-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7007008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c88072afd042ce8aa52e495e33f162534fedab86dfe135fde1ea2691c1890b24","compact":"33e4e388ba917430f092033e8a11cc95d3cf566827cbeddde634c94ed8e356f2","nasal":"33e4e388ba917430f092033e8a11cc95d3cf566827cbeddde634c94ed8e356f2"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-7-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":7,"verse":9,"english":"And dashing away (the Rākṣasa ranks) with his arrowy shower, even as the wind aroused dashes away a downpour, that best of male beings blew his mighty conch Pāñcajanya.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.662,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-7-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7007009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ab0590d84eaa506a5bd6ef4cb887d306394946d1f5d85f2a97a8cbf814a95a80","compact":"ba654c347d5e6a3ef7e5d488ed49020f70b7dc9d1949b6d58a94614f1c7b793d","nasal":"18d27a1a0f4a251d66036df2baa900b4c6dfefecc778489506def2e14ef2df6c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-7-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":7,"verse":10,"english":"Winded by Hari with his utmost might, that water-sprung king of conchs, endowed with terrific blares, roared, as if afflicting the three worlds.","alignmen