":"uttara","sarga":7,"verse":13,"english":"And dight with dainty feathered parts having heads, the shafts discharged from the śārnga, resembling thunder-bolts, riving those Rākşása, entered the earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.947,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-7-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7007013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"87448534b893e9c164da528a3e48b184557457092b5031ef109368debc3b8f7e","compact":"0bb78441b007bde9061efa3765b70111848ab0943823ea71f5e61411545f5d1d","nasal":"9f55de924f6c0e83ee784b581e8a2a5fc925a9ded7b3e4a0a2ee63877426cd89"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-7-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":7,"verse":14,"english":"In that conflict, pierced by the arrows discharged from Nārāyana's arm, the Rākşasa began to drop to the ground like mountains struck with the thunder-bolt.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.444,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-7-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7007014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d2b013d1d9cdd0f465eb142fa1c84f64b94bb3c0d0c634dcf37d66cdb34ff6fb","compact":"ccabe67297a013d32a179be44c60021f9f0120d64b19a7308b0fe7fbd8dbf5b6","nasal":"ccabe67297a013d32a179be44c60021f9f0120d64b19a7308b0fe7fbd8dbf5b6"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-7-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":7,"verse":15,"english":"The wounds on the persons of the foes inflicted by the discus of Vişnu discharge blood in streams, like mountains discharging streams of red chalk.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.354,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-7-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7007015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1e0e17d712387f03f354af707a9dee48a3dfdba753735e0cf3b0d66b6e73a9c9","compact":"89f9f4531b79b2